# Text files are stored with LF line endings in git, and eol=lf also checks
# them out with LF in every working tree. That overrides core.autocrlf, so
# Windows checkouts get LF rather than CRLF. Editors that handle LF need no
# change; to keep CRLF checkouts instead, this line would become
# "* text=auto".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# The root index.html used to be stored with mixed line endings and needed an
# exemption here. The owner's commits after b607af9 converted it to LF
# (2,189 lines, no CRLF), so the rule above already matches it and no
# exemption is needed.
